    "schema_version": "1.2.0",
    "claim_id": "claim:monstera:lighting:001",
    "plant_id": "plant:monstera",
    "plant_name": "Monstera",
    "scientific_name": "Monstera deliciosa",
    "entity_scope": "common_name_mapping",
    "dimension": "lighting",
    "qualifiers": {
      "environment": "indoor"
    },
    "claim_text": "Provide moderate brightness without direct sunlight; variegated cultivars need more light than dark-green cultivars.",
    "source_id": "ncsu:monstera-deliciosa",
    "source_title": "Monstera deliciosa",
    "source_type": "extension",
    "authority_for": [
      "horticultural_care"
    ],
    "locator": {
      "url": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/monstera-deliciosa/",
      "section": "Description",
      "paragraph": "Indoor care paragraph"
    },
    "review_status": "rejected",
    "accessed_at": "2026-08-12",
    "review_notes": "Mapping cannot be verified from this page and the page argues against a blanket one: it lists Monstera adansonii and Rhaphidophora tetrasperma as commonly confused, and adansonii is widely sold as \"Monstera\" with different care needs. Confirm what the dataset's Monstera plant_id actually covers before approving a common_name_mapping record; if the entry is undifferentiated, this needs a narrower scope or a species-level split. Also drop environment: indoor — the source sentence (temperature, moderate brightness, humidity) carries no indoor limit, consistent with the rule applied elsewhere. Locator is Description paragraph 2. Noted, no action: the same sentence's temperature (60-85F) and humidity content has no dimension in the enum; the cultivar clause is cultivar-scoped inside a common_name_mapping record but stays acceptable as lighting."
  },
  {
    "schema_version": "1.2.0",
    "claim_id": "claim:monstera:watering:001",
    "plant_id": "plant:monstera",
    "plant_name": "Monstera",
    "scientific_name": "Monstera deliciosa",
    "entity_scope": "common_name_mapping",
    "dimension": "watering",
    "qualifiers": {
      "environment": "indoor"
    },
    "claim_text": "Water thoroughly, then allow the top quarter to one-third of the potting medium to dry before watering again.",
    "source_id": "ncsu:monstera-deliciosa",
    "source_title": "Monstera deliciosa",
    "source_type": "extension",
    "authority_for": [
      "horticultural_care"
    ],
    "locator": {
      "url": "https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/monstera-deliciosa/",
      "section": "Description",
      "paragraph": "Indoor care paragraph"
    },
    "review_status": "rejected",
    "accessed_at": "2026-08-12",
    "review_notes": "Text is faithful (proportional range and sequence preserved; \"of the potting medium\" is the only reasonable reading of the source's \"top quarter to one-third part\"). Same two fixes as claim:monstera:lighting:001 — drop environment: indoor, since this sentence carries no indoor limit and the \"dry interior settings\" phrase belongs to the following humidity sentence; and set locator to Description paragraph 2. Blocked on the same unresolved question: whether the dataset's Monstera entry covers only M. deliciosa. This claim carries more practical risk than the lighting one if it does not, since M. adansonii has thinner leaves and dries faster than this drying depth assumes."
  },
